{"id":"COR-2135","uuid":"67def213-541d-42f9-afe0-744347d99fe4","title":"memory notify --json: checkpoint work-launch failure bypasses the warning field","description":"In `entire-brain memory notify` (`internal/cli/memory_cmd.go`, shipped in PR #377 / <issue id="41ca52f6-58da-4f99-b940-cc2b470c9db8" href="https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-2127/checkpoint-event-host-brainnotify-plugin-detached-fact-store-upload">COR-2127</issue>), the `memoryWorkerLaunch` failure goes into the `warning` variable, which reaches both the text output and the `--json` payload. The sibling `memoryCheckpointWorkLaunch` failure is written straight to stderr with `Fprintf`, so a host adapter calling `memory notify --json` — exactly how the cli's brainnotify half consumes it — never sees that failure class in machine-readable output.

